@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-amount`
IMPORT `g6-payment`
IMPORT `g6-warning`
IMPORT `g6-appeal-and-publication`

-- g6-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT TO FAIL.
-- Each asserts the answer of a reading that FRAGMENT-G6.md registers as a fork and rejects, run against the function
-- that takes the reading chosen.  So each must fail while the encoding takes the other reading, and this file is
-- the proof that this harness can fail.  The count of failures is 40 (RED_EXPECTED in work/g6/check-g6.sh, and in
-- the FRAGMENT).  None of them may be refused or error in any other way.  The reading each one asserts is named in
-- the comment above it, with the fork's id.
-- The deontic alternatives (F-NOTICE, F-MUST54) cannot be asserted (a DEONTIC does not compare); they are traced in
-- the tests of their own modules.  The third reading of a dash (F-DASH: no sanction may be imposed) cannot be asserted
-- as a failing comparison either, because the reading taken REFUSES there and a refusal is reported as refused, not
-- failed; its alternative function is exercised in g6-tests-schedule-three.l4.

§ `Assertions meant to fail: the answers of the readings the encoding rejects`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an individual violator`  MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-IND", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`a corporate violator`    MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-CORP", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`violation (1)` MEANS `work with no licence at all`
`violation (2)` MEANS `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
`violation (3)` MEANS `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`
`violation (5)` MEANS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`

GIVEN who IS A Person
      item IS A `Listed violation`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Violation
`a violation by` who `of` item `on` day MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS item
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS day

`no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY
`Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 4 2), (YMD 2027 4 3)
`Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest`  MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 7 2), (YMD 2027 7 3)
`Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 7 16), (YMD 2027 7 17)
`Saturday 10 April 2027 as a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 4 10)
`Friday 16 and Saturday 17 March 2029 as days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2029 3 16), (YMD 2029 3 17)

-- Positional fields of `Notice of intention`: delivered on, in writing, act+date, amount, period (days), right,
-- deemed demand, power to add, intention to publish name.
`a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`an extension to 10 May 2027 without reasons recorded` MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 5 10, FALSE)
`an extension to Saturday 10 April 2027 with reasons recorded` MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 4 10, TRUE)

-- Positional fields of `Previous violation`: violator, violation, date of the act, sanction imposed, convicted.
`an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned` MEANS `Previous violation` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 16, TRUE, FALSE

-- Positional fields of `Administrative warning`: violator, violation, delivered on, states act+date, tells to stop, warns,
-- states the right to ask for cancellation, cancelled.
`a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled`        MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

`the index readings` MEANS
    LIST (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 10, YMD 2024 11 15,  99.8)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 11, YMD 2024 12 15, 100.0)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 12, YMD 2025 1 15,  100.4)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2025, 11, YMD 2025 12 15, 101.7)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2025, 12, YMD 2026 1 15,  101.9)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2026, 11, YMD 2026 12 15, 103.4)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2026, 12, YMD 2027 1 15,  103.6)

§§ `F-DASH: the dash of the corporation column (trap T14)`

-- 1. A dash read as the individual amount: the column B cell for a corporation at item (1) would be 20,000.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (1)` EQUALS JUST 20_000
-- 2. A dash read as zero.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (1)` EQUALS JUST 0

§§ `F-CAP: the cap of s 41(b) also bounds what is payable (trap T15)`

-- 3. Corporation, item (5), repeat, six months: held to the cap it would be 80,000; the reading taken gives 84,800.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 6 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 80_000

§§ `The s.10(c) forks: the answers without it, against the functions that apply it (kinds W and D)`

-- 4. s.43 (kind W): without s.10(c) the last day is Friday 2 April 2027; the reading taken gives Sunday 4 April.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` (YMD 2027 3 3) `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
-- 5. s.53(a) (kind W).
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the last day of the 30 days from` (YMD 2027 3 3) `with` `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 April 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 2
-- 6. s.56(a) (kind W): without s.10(c) the last day is Saturday 17 July 2027; the reading taken gives Sunday 18 July.
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `Friday 16 and Saturday 17 July 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
-- 7. s.48 (kind D): without s.10(c) the last day is Friday 2 July 2027; the reading taken gives Sunday 4 July.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2027 6 2) `Friday 2 and Saturday 3 July 2027 as days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 2
-- 8. s.57(e) (kind V): applying s.10(c) to a period of validity moves the end of an individual's publication
--    published on 3 September 2027 from 3 September 2029 to 4 September 2029 if that day is a holiday.
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 9 3) `for` `an individual` EQUALS YMD 2029 9 4

§§ `F-EXT, F-X and F-C: extensions of the s.43 period, and the day the notice is treated as a demand`

-- 9. F-EXT: an extension without recorded reasons counted.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `an extension to 10 May 2027 without reasons recorded` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 10
-- 10. F-X, F-C: s.10(c) applied to an extension that ends on a day of rest: 11 April; the reading taken gives 10 April.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `an extension to Saturday 10 April 2027 with reasons recorded` `Saturday 10 April 2027 as a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 11
-- 11. F-DEEMED: the notice treated as a demand delivered on the day AFTER the s.43 period ends.
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 3
-- 12. F-DEEMED: the notice treated as a demand delivered on the day the notice was delivered.
#ASSERT `s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 3

§§ `F-MONTHS, F-START: the count of months of a continuing violation`

-- 13. Calendar months touched, 15 March to 14 June 2027: four; the reading taken counts two completed months.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14) EQUALS 4
-- 14. Calendar months touched after the first: three.
#ASSERT `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (YMD 2027 3 15) `to` (YMD 2027 6 14) EQUALS 3
-- 15. F-START: counted from the delivery of the warning (2 months) rather than from the day the breach began (3).
#ASSERT `s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the day the breach began` (YMD 2027 2 10) `until` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS 2

§§ `F-SAME, F-WINDOW: a repeat violation (trap T17)`

-- 16. F-SAME: read by Third Schedule item, an item (2) violation after an item (1) violation is NOT a repeat.
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (2)` `on` (YMD 2028 6 1)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
-- 17. F-WINDOW (s.45(b), kind B read as W): with s.10(c) applied, a violation on Sunday 18 March 2029 is still inside the
--     window that the reading taken ends on Friday 16 March 2029.
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 18)) `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `an earlier item (1) violation on 16 March 2027, sanctioned`)
-- 18. F-WINDOW (s.54(b)): with s.10(c) applied, a further violation on Sunday 4 March 2029 is inside the window that the
--     reading taken ends on Saturday 3 March 2029.
#ASSERT `s 54(b) — the further violation after` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `is treated as a repeat violation:` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2029 3 4))
-- 19. F-CANCEL: a cancelled warning still makes a continued breach a continuing violation.
#ASSERT `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `a complete warning on item (1) that was cancelled` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (1)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE

§§ `F-BASE, F-CHAIN, F-ROUND, F-FIRST, F-R: the amount and its update`

-- 20. F-BASE: the additions computed on the amount as enacted, then updated: 5,290; the reading taken gives 5,293.6.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (3)` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) 2 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 5_290
-- 21. F-CHAIN: rounding once at the end, 5,170; the reading taken (each year's rounded amount carried on) gives 5,180.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 5_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 5_170
-- 22. F-ROUND: a half going to the even multiple, 5,080; the reading taken (half up) gives 5,090.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` 5_085 EQUALS 5_080
-- 23. F-FIRST: the first update in 2028 (after Chapter 6 commences), the amount on 1 June 2027 is still 20,000; with the first
--     update in 2026 it is 20,680.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_000
-- 24. F-R: the update not yet in effect on Saturday 2 January 2027 (moved past 1 and 2 January): the amount is still 20,340.
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the amount of` 20_000 `updated on` (YMD 2027 1 2) `, the first update being in` 2026 `and the index readings being` `the index readings` EQUALS 20_340

§§ `F-DAY, F-PERIOD, F-ANCHOR, F-APPEAL-DEEMED, F-FLOOR, F-INTEREST`

-- 25. F-DAY: for a violator who made no representations and whose stayed appeal was decided, the demand's day before the
--     appeal's: the notice day.  The reading taken answers with the day of the decision on the appeal.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 4 2)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2028 2 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 3)
-- 26. F-PERIOD: the 45 days the demand states govern over s.48's 30: the last day would be 17 July 2027, not 2 July.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2027 6 2) `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
-- 27. F-ANCHOR: the 30 days of s.53(a) counted from the day of the breach (10 February 2027): 12 March 2027.
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 12
-- 28. F-APPEAL-DEEMED: for a violator who made no representations, the day notice of the decision counts as delivered is
--     the day the notice of intention was delivered, 3 March 2027, not the day it is treated as a demand, 2 April 2027.
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day notice of the decision counts as delivered to a violator who made no representations` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 3
-- 29. F-FLOOR: the amounts fixed counting only column B, so a sanction of 30,000 for a repeat item (5) is not below the floor.
#ASSERT `s 46(a) — a sanction of` 30_000 `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` (`s 46(a) — the amounts fixed under the subchapter for the violation, additions included` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 0 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings`)
-- 30. F-INTEREST: the rates reading, 20,000 x (1 + 0.01 + 0.005) = 20,300; the amounts reading with 150 and 50 gives 20,200.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 20_000 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` (JUST 150) `and arrears fees` (JUST 50) EQUALS 20_300

§§ `F-ADD: the additions at the Commissioner's discretion (s.42(b)(4) against s.45)`

-- 31. The Commissioner declines to add: the fixed sanction alone, 20,000; the reading taken adds them, 40,800.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) 2 TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_000

§§ `F-ACTDAY, F-SHORTEN, F-NOTICE: the first reading of the s.43, s.48, s.53 and s.56 windows, and of the s.44 deeming`

-- These five readings were the encoding's own until the independent test author (ind-c) showed them wrong; the assertions
-- that encoded them were moved here from the tests of their own modules, unchanged, and the readings are now the callable
-- alternatives.  Each fails against the reading taken.
`an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` MEANS JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` OF YMD 2027 3 20, TRUE)
`a notice silent on the right to argue and its consequence` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- 32. F-ACTDAY, s.43: representations made on the day the notice is delivered are late (the period starts the day after).
--     The reading taken: they are within the 30 days.
#ASSERT NOT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2027 3 3) `is within the period for representations of` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all`
-- 33. F-ACTDAY, s.43 and s.44(d): the violator did not make his representations within the period when he made them on the
--     day of delivery.
#ASSERT NOT `s 43, s 44(d) — the violator made his representations within the period` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 3))
-- 34. F-ACTDAY, s.53(a): a request to cancel made on the day the warning is delivered is late.
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` NOTHING `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- 35. F-ACTDAY, s.56(a): an appeal filed on the day notice of the decision is delivered is late.
#ASSERT NOT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- 36. F-ACTDAY, s.48: a payment made on the day the demand is delivered is late.
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- 37. F-SHORTEN, s.43: an extension to 20 March 2027 makes 20 March the last day, although the 30 days run to 2 April.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 20
-- 38. F-SHORTEN, s.53(b): the same for a request to cancel a warning.
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a complete warning on item (1) delivered on 3 March 2027` `counting from its delivery, given` `an extension to 20 March 2027 with reasons recorded` `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 20
-- 39. F-NOTICE, s.44(d): a notice that omits the statements s.42(b)(3) requires is still treated as a payment demand
--     delivered at the end of the s.43 period, 2 April 2027, when no representations are made; the reading taken gives NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` `a notice silent on the right to argue and its consequence` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 4 2)
-- 40. F-ACTDAY, with its consequence under s.44(d): a violator who made his representations on the day of delivery is
--     treated as having made none, so the notice is treated as a demand on 2 April 2027; the reading taken gives NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING (`s 43, s 44(d) — the violator made his representations within the period` `a complete notice of intention delivered on 3 March 2027` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 3))) NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 4 2)
